    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We present a new 3D slip inversion method based on angular dislocation in a linear-elastic, homogeneous and isotropic whole- or half-space using planar, triangular elements of displacement discontinuity and the boundary element method (BEM). This method, based on Poly3D, uses complex 3D fault surfaces geometry, and is a major advance compare to existing codes.\r\n\r\nIn this contribution, the theory is explained and a validation across synthetic cases is presented. Finally, a real case is studied and the result is compared to an existing solution using rectangular dislocations, showing the advantages of this new method. Industry applications are discussed in the next contribution of this volume.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
